Seam: chrome/browser/sessions/BUILD.gn, source_set("impl") — the target
      session_service.cc actually builds in, not source_set("sessions").
Why: GN wiring for patch 0130. The hook includes an //arcium/browser header
     and //chrome/browser/sessions has no Arcium dep at all. `gn check` on
     that target is what says whether this is still needed after a rebase.

     No cycle: //chrome/browser/sessions does not reach //chrome/browser/ui:ui,
     and //arcium/browser depends on nothing under //chrome.

     Patch 0120's seam needs no companion hunk here. //chrome/browser/ui:ui
     already depends on //arcium/ui/browser (patch 0010), and //arcium/browser
     is a public_dep of that target — correctly so, since its own headers
     include tab_binding.h and archive_store.h — so it transits. Adding a
     second dep line to chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn was tried and rejected: it
     lands inside patch 0010's hunk context, which breaks 0010's
     already-applied check and makes scripts/sync non-idempotent.
Delegates to: nothing. GN wiring carries no call.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/sessions/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/sessions/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/sessions/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/sessions/BUILD.gn
@@ -122,6 +122,8 @@
     ]
 
     deps += [
+      # Arcium: session_service.cc calls arcium::AppendTabEntryCommand.
+      "//arcium/browser",
       "//chrome/browser:after_startup_task_utils",
       "//chrome/browser/content_settings:content_settings_factory",
       "//chrome/browser/devtools",
